= Bias–variance tradeoff — Technical =

== Squared-error decomposition ==
For response:

<pre>
Y = f(X) + ε
E[ε|X] = 0
Var(ε|X) = σ²
</pre>

and estimator f_hat trained on random sample S, pointwise expected squared error can be decomposed as:

<pre>
E_S,ε[(Y - f_hat(X))²]
= bias² + variance + σ²
</pre>

under the usual setup.

== Scope ==
The exact decomposition depends on loss and statistical assumptions.

Classification, non-squared losses, adaptive pipelines, and structured prediction require related but different analyses.

== Double descent ==
Interpolation-era models can show:

<pre>
classical descent
→ interpolation peak
→ second descent
</pre>

as capacity increases.

This does not invalidate bias/variance concepts; it invalidates treating one monotonic capacity-to-variance story as universal.

